{"File":"/Users/admin/Documents/member-callout-exercise/DESIGN.md","LineNumber":15,"LineContent":"Hi Denise, sorry about Thursday. Here’s what we’ll build. When you send a callout, every member of your local gets it in the app, and it waits there until their phone has signal, so a day underground doesn’t mean missing it. The phone notification is just a nudge on top. You’ll see how many members have received it, opened it, and replied *Coming* or *Can’t make it*. The numbers refresh every few minutes, and you can refresh them yourself right before you leave the hall. Resending a callout will never give anyone a second copy. And nobody outside your local can see your members’ contact info, apprentices included. We’ll confirm that isn’t happening today either."}
{"File":"/Users/admin/Documents/member-callout-exercise/DESIGN.md","LineNumber":19,"LineContent":"* **Scope:** Leaders send callouts and see results for their own local only. Each member belongs to one local for now."}
{"File":"/Users/admin/Documents/member-callout-exercise/DESIGN.md","LineNumber":75,"LineContent":"  status                   -- draft | sending | sent | closed"}
{"File":"/Users/admin/Documents/member-callout-exercise/DESIGN.md","LineNumber":94,"LineContent":"* **Who it went to:** When a send starts, I create one recipient row for every active member of that local. A missing row means the member was never targeted, and a row with every field empty means “nothing happened”. I rejected creating rows lazily when members open the app, because then “nothing” can’t be counted and a restarted push worker has no record of who was already pushed."}
{"File":"/Users/admin/Documents/member-callout-exercise/DESIGN.md","LineNumber":101,"LineContent":"### 2. The Send Path"}
{"File":"/Users/admin/Documents/member-callout-exercise/DESIGN.md","LineNumber":104,"LineContent":"1. The leader presses Send. The request carries an idempotency key. The server loads the announcement scoped to the leader’s own local and checks that they hold a leadership role there."}
